  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Duvoglustat and Serine/threonine-protein kinase D2 through a series of target interactions. Duvoglustat is implicated in targeting Cell division cycle 2-like protein kinase 6, which is in turn targeted by multiple compounds, including 3-(1S,2R-Dihydroxypropyl)-1,6,8-Trihydroxyanthracene-9,10-Dione, Dehydrobruceine B, and 1-deoxymannojirimycin. These compounds all share a common target of Serine/threonine-protein kinase D2, indicating a possible pathway where Duvoglustat may influence the activity of this kinase through its interaction with the intermediate protein kinase 6. The cumulative scores from the three paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, supported by the shared targets and the presence of multiple compounds that converge on the same downstream effect. The evidence highlights a mechanistic link between Duvoglustat and the kinase D2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
